NAME
    glob - filename wildcard match (#include "../lib_glob.c")

SYNOPSIS
    #include "../lib_glob.c"
    if (gmatch(pattern, name)) ...

DESCRIPTION
    gmatch(p, s) is 1 when the pattern p matches the WHOLE name s, else
    0:
        *    any run of characters, none included
        ?    exactly one character
    Any other character matches itself with the case folded, so *.txt
    finds README.TXT (Y1/OS names are case-sensitive, a pattern is
    not). No I/O and no globals; gfold(c) is the upper-casing it uses.

    To turn a pattern into the list of matching files of a directory,
    use globx on top of it.

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: the P8X gmatch recursed on every
    suffix after a *, which y1cc rejects (static frames, no recursion).
    This is the classic iterative match with one backtrack point:
    remember the last * and how much of s it has eaten, and on a
    mismatch let it eat one more character. Same results, no stack.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/lib_glob.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    globx, stdin, find, dir
